## Authentication and Authorization

This feature follows the platform authorization convention:

```text
Entra app role value = platform permission
```

The feature backend does not maintain role-permission mappings.

Do not add local mappings such as:

```text
developer → [[ names.feature_key ]].view
admin → *
access_as_user → [[ names.feature_key ]].view
```

OAuth scopes are used for API access. They are not business permissions.

---

## Permission Naming

Use this convention:

```text
<feature-key>.<action>
```

Recommended permissions for this feature:

```text
[[ names.feature_key ]].view
[[ names.feature_key ]].create
[[ names.feature_key ]].edit
[[ names.feature_key ]].delete
[[ names.feature_key ]].manage
```

Platform-wide admin:

```text
platform.admin
```

`platform.admin` grants wildcard access.

---

## Backend Permission Enforcement

Generated backend endpoints should use:

```python
from fastapi import Depends
from app.platform.auth_context import AuthContext
from app.platform.permissions import require_permissions


@router.get("/items")
async def list_items(
    ctx: AuthContext = Depends(require_permissions(["[[ names.feature_key ]].view"])),
):
    return {"items": []}
```

For one-of-many checks:

```python
from app.platform.permissions import require_any_permission


@router.post("/items")
async def save_item(
    ctx: AuthContext = Depends(
        require_any_permission([
            "[[ names.feature_key ]].edit",
            "[[ names.feature_key ]].manage",
        ])
    ),
):
    return {"status": "saved"}
```

Authorization responsibility is split as follows:

| Layer | Responsibility |
|---|---|
| Entra | Assign roles to users/groups |
| Bootstrap API | Filter visible features |
| Shell | Render accessible navigation |
| Feature frontend | UX gating only |
| Feature backend | Security enforcement |

