## Local Mock Auth

Local development defaults to mock auth:

```env
AUTH_MODE=mock
AUTH_DEFAULT_DEV_ROLES_RAW=[[ names.feature_key ]].view
AUTH_DEBUG_HEADERS_ENABLED=true
```

Optional debug header:

```http
X-Debug-Roles: [[ names.feature_key ]].view,[[ names.feature_key ]].edit
```

This allows local testing without Entra.

Debug headers must not be enabled in production.

---

## Production Auth

Production must use Entra:

```env
APP_ENVIRONMENT=production
AUTH_MODE=entra
AUTH_DEBUG_HEADERS_ENABLED=false
```

Required settings:

```env
ENTRA_TENANT_ID=<tenant-id>
ENTRA_AUDIENCE=api://<bootstrap-api-client-id>
ENTRA_ISSUER=https://login.microsoftonline.com/<tenant-id>/v2.0
ENTRA_JWKS_URL=https://login.microsoftonline.com/<tenant-id>/discovery/v2.0/keys
```

The token must contain a `roles` claim with permission-shaped values.

Example:

```json
{
  "roles": [
    "[[ names.feature_key ]].view",
    "[[ names.feature_key ]].edit"
  ]
}
```

---

## Frontend Authorization

The frontend receives Shell context at mount time.

Frontend authorization is only for user experience.

Use permissions to:

```text
hide unavailable buttons
disable unavailable actions
adjust visible navigation inside the feature
```

Do not rely on frontend checks for security.

Backend endpoints must enforce permissions independently.

